# Hugging Face ZeroGPU Space (Gradio SDK, Python 3.12.12) -- see docs/ZEROGPU.md.
# Compiled to requirements.txt with constraints from backend/requirements.lock, so every shared package keeps the
# version tested in development. Two documented exceptions:
#   torch 2.13.0 (CUDA build): newest version on ZeroGPU's documented list; `import spaces` needs a CUDA build of torch
#     (it reads torch.version.cuda). Inference still runs on CPU. Measured bit-identical to the evaluated results.
#   pillow 12.x: gradio requires <13 (dev lock has 13.0.0 via matplotlib); not on the inference path.
#   pydantic 2.12.x: the Hugging Face Gradio-SDK build installs this file TOGETHER with
#     `gradio[oauth,mcp]==<sdk_version>` (see deploy/zerogpu/check_hf_build.py). The `mcp` extra requires
#     pydantic>=2.11.10,<=2.12.5, so the extras are locked here too (deployment attempt 1 failed on pydantic==2.14.3).
torch==2.13.0
neuraloperator==2.0.0
numpy
fastapi
uvicorn
pydantic
matplotlib
gradio[oauth,mcp]==6.30.0
spaces==0.51.3
